{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan review PASS (signed, 0 blocking, 2 advisory). Recording the accepted E4 advisory here rather than by a description edit, which would invalidate the fresh attestation.\n\nE4 advisory ACCEPTED and corrected: the title's '800/800' and the Context's '799' are HISTORICAL — they describe the state when bug c083 landed. The authoritative CURRENT baseline is `origin/main` @ c3fb869ab5: `wc -l src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py` = 794, i.e. 6 lines under the strictly-greater 800 gate, not zero. The reviewer is right that this is not an already-blocking cap today.\n\nThe split is still justified, on the grounds the module-size policy actually states: AGENTS.md targets **200-500 LOC per file** with 800 as an absolute backstop. At 794 the file is ~59% over the top of the target band and has repeatedly forced documentation to be deleted to buy lines (c083). This work is proactive target-band compliance, not an emergency unblock. AC1 (<700) is unchanged and remains the measurable outcome.\n\nP6 advisory NOT applied: it lints the shared verify-command registry (52 of 53 checks abstained) and does not describe this ticket's ACs; no verify_commands are set on this ticket.\n\nSeam decided (see the updated Approach): extract `remediation_mode_candidate` + its sole private helper `_sidecar_branch_decision` to a new sibling `remediation_mode.py`. Reference set confirmed by BOTH Serena `find_referencing_symbols` and a repo-wide string `grep`: `_sidecar_branch_decision` has exactly one caller (the function directly above it); `remediation_mode_candidate` is reached only as the module attribute `attest.remediation_mode_candidate`, including one `monkeypatch.setattr` target, so a re-export preserves every site."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785893170285027001,"uuid":"88e02cba-a73c-4765-b81c-37677374d4c7"}